hadiths[69]{hadithnumber,text}:
"749","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When a man comes with a messenger, that itself is his permission."
"750","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The name of Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) was Barrah, so it was said: She considers herself pious, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) named her Zainab."
"751","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The name of Zaynab or Maymunah was Barrah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) changed her name to Zaynab or Maymunah."
"752","Makhul (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Of all good deeds, the reward that comes most quickly is for righteousness and maintaining family ties, and of all evil, the punishment that comes most quickly is for oppression and a wicked, forceful oath; it leaves houses deserted.”"
"753","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""There was a tree on the road which was a cause of trouble for the people, so a man cut it down and removed it from the path. Because of this, he was forgiven and admitted into Paradise."
"754","Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) a similar narration and reported this addition: She (Sayyidah Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her) stated that I said: O Messenger of Allah! You have said what you had to say, then you honored him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The worst people in the sight of Allah are those who are honored in order to be safe from their evil."
"755","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman entered Hell because of a cat. She had tied it up, so she neither fed it nor gave it water, nor did she let it go so that it could eat the insects of the earth."
"756","Muhammad bin Ja'far narrated with this chain: He said: A woman went to Hell because of a cat; she had tied it up and did not let it go so that it could eat the insects of the earth."
"757","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When any of you fights, he should avoid (striking) the face."
"758","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When any of you fights, he should avoid the face."
"759","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that I said: O Messenger of Allah! When I visit you, my heart becomes happy and my eyes are cooled. Please tell me about everything. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Everything has been created from water."" I said: Tell me about an act which, if I perform it, I will enter Paradise. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Spread peace (greetings), feed (others), maintain ties of kinship, and stand in prayer at night (tahajjud) while people are sleeping, and you will enter Paradise in peace."
"760","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Jibreel (peace be upon him) continued to advise me regarding the neighbor until I thought he would make him an heir.”"
"761","Khalid Qaisi narrated: I said: O Abu Huraira! Have you heard anything from your beloved (peace be upon him) by which we may comfort our hearts? He replied: Yes! I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) say: ""Your little children are the insects of Paradise."
"762","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A woman came to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) with her son. She said: O Messenger of Allah! I fear for him, as I have already sent three children ahead (i.e., they have died). The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""You have indeed built a very strong barrier against Hellfire."
"763","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked: Who is most deserving of my good conduct? The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: ""Your mother."" He asked: Then who? The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: ""Then your mother."" He asked: Then who? The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: ""Then still your mother."" He asked: Then who? The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: ""Your father."
"764","Hazrat Abu Zar’ah narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"765","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever names (his child) after my name, then he should not take my kunyah, and whoever takes my kunyah, then he should not name (his child) after my name."
"766","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should not harm his neighbor, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest."" It was asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is the right of the guest? He (peace be upon him) said: ""Three (days is the right of hospitality), so whatever is more than these (three days) or after them, that is charity. And whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, if any matter presents itself to him, he should speak good or remain silent. Accept the advice of goodness regarding women, for they have been created from a rib, and the most crooked part of the rib is its upper part. If you try to straighten it, you will break it, and if you leave it, it will remain crooked. So accept the advice of goodness regarding women."
"767","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""It is obligatory for every Muslim to give charity every day."" They asked: O Messenger of Allah! Who has the ability to do this? He (peace be upon him) said: ""Removing something harmful from the road is charity, guiding a Muslim on the way is charity, visiting a sick Muslim is charity, participating in a funeral is charity, replying to the greeting of a Muslim is charity."" Muhammad bin Fudayl bin Ghazwan narrated a similar narration with this chain, the narrator stated: They said: Who has the ability to do this? He (peace be upon him) said: ""Removing something harmful from the road is charity, visiting a sick person is charity, participating in a funeral is charity, enjoining good and forbidding evil is charity, replying to the greeting of a Muslim is charity."
"768","Muhammad bin Fudayl bin Ghazwan narrated with this chain a similar narration. The narrator stated: They said: Who has the strength for this? The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Your removing something harmful from the road is charity, your visiting the sick is charity, your attending a funeral is charity, your enjoining good and forbidding evil is charity, your returning the greeting of a Muslim is charity."
"769","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""It is obligatory for every Muslim to give charity every day."" They asked: O Messenger of Allah! Who has the ability to do this? He (peace be upon him) said: ""Guiding a Muslim on the road is charity, replying to a Muslim's greeting is charity, enjoining good and forbidding evil is charity."
"770","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""I am a human being; just as a human becomes angry, I also become angry, and I curse just as a human curses. So, if I have ever spoken harshly to any person/slave or cursed him who was not deserving of it, then (O Allah) make it a mercy for him."
"771","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: My beloved friend, the one of the chamber, Abu al-Qasim (peace be upon him) said: ""Mercy is taken away from the unfortunate person."
"772","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): Such-and-such woman prays Tahajjud at night and fasts during the day, but she harms her neighbor. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""She is in Hell."" It was said to him: Such-and-such woman performs the obligatory prayers, fasts in Ramadan, gives a few pieces of cheese in charity and has nothing else, and she does not harm anyone. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""She is in Paradise."
"773","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: It was said: O Messenger of Allah! Such-and-such woman offers Tahajjud prayer, the narrator stated: Then I narrated it to them just as Jarir narrated it to us, so Abu Usamah affirmed it and said: Yes."
"774","Abdullah narrated: For any of you to have his belly filled with pus is better for him than to have it filled with poetry. Atiq narrated: I mentioned this to Yazid bin Al-Asam, so he said: I heard Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) mention the same from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."
"775","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""A Muslim has a right over another Muslim that when he meets him, he should greet him with salam; when he sneezes and says «الحمدللہ» , he should reply to him with «يرحمك الله» ; when he invites him, he should accept his invitation; when he falls ill, he should visit him; when he dies, he should attend his funeral, and in his absence, he should wish well for him."
"776","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Among the worst qualities a person can have are greed, miserliness, and being cowardly fearful."
"777","The narrator reported: Al-Mala'i narrated to us with this chain in the same manner."
"778","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""A man is upon the religion of his close friend, so let one of you look at whom he befriends."
"779","Abu Awn Al-A'war narrated: Whenever a believer says something good, the next thing he says is even gentler than the previous one."
"780","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when a man sneezed and said: «الحمدللہ» , so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: «يرحمك الله» . Then another man sneezed, but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not say anything to him. So he said: O Messenger of Allah! You responded to that man, but you did not say anything to me. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: ""He praised Allah, whereas you remained silent."
"781","Abdur-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, who said: Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The one who strives for the widow and the poor is like the one who fights in the way of Allah. And I and the sponsor of the orphan will be like this,"" and he gestured with his index and middle fingers."
"782","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The one who looks after widows and the poor is like the one who fights in the way of Allah. I and the one who takes care of an orphan will be like this (in Paradise)."" He (peace be upon him) indicated with his index and middle fingers."
"783","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""When Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibril (peace be upon him) and says: 'Allah loves so-and-so, so love him.' Then Jibril (peace be upon him) calls out to the inhabitants of the heavens: 'Allah loves so-and-so, so love him.' Then acceptance is placed for him among the people of the earth."
"784","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""It is sufficient for a person to be considered bad that his religion or his worldly affairs are pointed out, except for the one whom Allah protects."
"785","It is narrated with the same chain that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah does not look at your appearances nor at your wealth, but He looks at your hearts and your deeds."
"786","With this (previous) chain, Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The outcome of deceit, trickery, and fraud is Hell."
"787","With this (previous) chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “To deny the truth and to consider other people insignificant is part of arrogance.”"
"788","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fulfills the need of his believing brother is like the one who has spent his life in the service of Allah."
"789","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abusing a Muslim is wickedness and killing him is disbelief."
"790","With this same chain (as previous): The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Allah shows mercy to every merciful person.” The Companions said: O Messenger of Allah! Each of us shows mercy to himself. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “None of you truly shows mercy to himself until he shows mercy to the people.”"
"791","With the same (previous) chain of narration, it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Allah has revealed to me that you should adopt humility, and that you should not wrong one another."
"792","Saeed bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A believer is not bitten from the same hole twice."
"793","Saeed (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to this."
"794","With this (previous) chain, it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Indeed, Allah is gentle, He loves gentleness, and He grants through gentleness what He does not grant through harshness."
"795","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: When this verse was revealed: ""Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it,"" it was hard on the Muslims and caused them great distress. They complained about it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: ""Remain close and adopt moderation. Whatever hardship befalls a believer, it is an expiation for him, even if a thorn pricks him (that too is a cause for expiation)."
"796","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The rider should greet the one who is walking, the one who is walking should greet the one who is sitting, and the smaller group should greet the larger group."
"797","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The strong one is not the one who overcomes people, the strong one is the one who controls himself."
"798","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""A Muslim is the brother of another Muslim, he does not oppress him nor does he disgrace him."" Then he (peace be upon him) pointed towards his chest and said: ""Taqwa is here."
"799","With this same chain, it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The person with the most perfect faith among the people is the one whose character is the best among them."
"800","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul! You cannot enter Paradise until you become believers. And you cannot become believers until you love one another. Shall I not tell you about something which, if you do it, love will grow among you?"" They said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah!"" He (peace be upon him) said: ""Spread salam (greetings of peace) among yourselves."
"801","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Lying is permissible only in three matters: a man lies to his wife so that she may be pleased with him, a man lies to reconcile between people, and a man lies in war."
"802","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called the believing women for allegiance, so Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah! Will you not show your hand for us? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I do not shake hands with women."
"803","Sayyida Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever defends his (Muslim) brother in his absence, it is incumbent upon Allah to free him from Hell."
"804","Mujahid (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) named Lady Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) as Barrah, and this was because one day he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is Maymunah here?"" So they replied: No."
"805","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that a man was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he (peace be upon him) said: ""He is a bad man of the tribe."" Then that man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he spoke to him. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) giving him full attention, to the extent that I thought he had a high status with the Prophet."
"806","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Something struck Usama’s (may Allah be pleased with him) face and blood started to flow, so I washed his face and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wiped it with his shirt, and said: “Treat us well, while she is not a girl.” The narrator stated: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) looked at the face of Usama (may Allah be pleased with him) after the death of his father (Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him), he would weep."
"807","Narrated from Sayyida Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with her): She heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""He is not a liar who reconciles between people, conveying good or saying good things."
"808","Sayyidah Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""He is not a liar who reconciles between two people, he speaks good or conveys good."
"809","Umm Tariq, the freed slave woman of Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him), narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him), and he sought permission to enter. Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) remained silent. Then he sought permission again, and he remained silent again. Then he sought permission a third time, and he remained silent again, so he turned back. Then Sayyiduna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) sent me to him. When I reached the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I said to him: We only intended that you would increase us (in supplication for peace). She said: I heard the sound of someone seeking permission at the door, but I did not see anything. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Who are you?” She said: I am Umm Muldim. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “No welcome for you. Can you guide (us) to Quba?” She said: Yes. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Bring them.”"
"810","Sayyidah Umm Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in a marfu’ manner: He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Whoever has been given his portion of gentleness has been given his portion of goodness, and whoever is deprived of gentleness has been deprived of his portion of goodness to that extent.”"
"811","It is narrated from Zaid bin Aslam that Abdul Malik bin Marwan sent a message to Sayyida Umm Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with her) so that she would come to him. She called her servant, but he delayed in coming, so she cursed him. Then Sayyida Umm Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Do not curse him, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Those who curse excessively will neither be able to intercede nor bear witness before Allah on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"812","Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: It was asked from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) about the explanation of this verse: «ما أسألكم عليه من أجر إلا المودة في القربى» ""I do not ask you for any reward for this (invitation and preaching) except love for kinship."" So Saeed bin Jubair (may Allah have mercy on him) said: By kinship is meant the family of Muhammad (peace be upon him). Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: You have been hasty, you have been hasty, because the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was not from the offspring of Quraysh except that he had kinship among them, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Maintain the ties of kinship that exist between me and them."
"813","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Create ease, do not create hardship, create ease, hardship will not be imposed upon you. So when you become angry, remain silent, and when you become angry, adopt silence."
"814","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Teach, make things easy and do not make things difficult, instruct, make things easy and do not make things difficult, teach, make things easy and do not make things difficult."" Then he said: ""When you become angry, remain silent, when you become angry, remain silent, and when you become angry, remain silent."
"815","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the mosque one day, while he was gesturing with his hand in this manner. Maqri (the narrator) turned his hand in this way, and he (the Prophet) was saying: “Whoever grants respite to a debtor in difficulty (for repayment), or forgives him, Allah will save him from the steam/intensity of Hell. Listen! The deed of Paradise is like a hard place on a mound. Listen! The deed of Hell is easy on soft ground, and the truly fortunate person is the one who saves his soul. The sip of anger that a servant of Allah swallows is the most beloved sip to Allah. Whoever restrains (his anger), Allah fills his heart with faith.”"
"816","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The best among you is the one whose character is best among you."
"817","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: “Allah curses the one who sacrifices (an animal) in the name of other than Allah, Allah curses the one who changes the boundaries of the land, Allah curses the one who misleads a blind person from the path, Allah curses the one who abuses his parents, Allah curses the one who claims someone other than his masters as his master, Allah curses the one who does the act of the people of Lot, and Allah curses the one who does the act of the people of Lot.”"
